{"article":{"id":900005852323,"url":"https://pexels-help.zendesk.com/api/v2/help_center/en-us/articles/900005852323.json","html_url":"https://help.pexels.com/hc/en-us/articles/900005852323-How-do-I-get-unlimited-requests","author_id":402976000473,"comments_disabled":false,"draft":false,"promoted":false,"position":3,"vote_sum":153,"vote_count":211,"section_id":900001840183,"created_at":"2021-03-12T04:03:24Z","updated_at":"2026-09-06T13:58:51Z","name":"How do I get unlimited requests?","title":"How do I get unlimited requests?","source_locale":"en-us","locale":"en-us","outdated":false,"outdated_locales":[],"edited_at":"2021-06-04T15:23:42Z","user_segment_id":null,"permission_group_id":2553394,"content_tag_ids":[],"label_names":[],"body":"<p><strong>We're happy to remove the request limits on eligible applications but as this is our most asked question, we ask that you please review these requirements carefully.</strong></p>\n<p>Our API keys come with the default rate limit of 200/hour and 20,000/month. Removing these limits is completely free but your platform needs to be eligible and meet our requirements. </p>\n<h3>Eligibility</h3>\n<p>API users are bound to the same Terms and Conditions as Pexels users, which can be found in summary <a href=\"https://www.pexels.com/license/\" target=\"_self\">here</a>. The added condition for API partners is that you <span class=\"wysiwyg-underline\"><strong>may not</strong></span> copy our core functionality with the API. This includes:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Wallpaper apps</li>\n<li>Using our API then promoting your site as a free stock platform</li>\n<li>Enabling the selling of unaltered copies of a photo or video, (e.g. as a poster, print or on a physical product without modifying it first). </li>\n</ul>\n<p>Essentially, we look to ensure you're using our API to add a feature or build on an existing app or website that provides value beyond just our API. If you're looking to build an app or plug-in for a program (ie. WordPress, Figma, etc.) get in touch with us. We're happy to support (and even <a href=\"https://www.pexels.com/pro/\" target=\"_self\">feature</a>) community-built projects but we need to approve them first. </p>\n<h3>Requirements</h3>\n<p>Pexels and our contributors must be credited within your platform. To verify this, we require either a mock-up, video or demo of how Pexels and the photographers are credited within your platform. You can review our guidelines <a href=\"https://www.pexels.com/api/documentation/#guidelines\" target=\"_self\">here</a> and there are screenshots attached to this FAQ as examples. </p>\n<p> </p>\n<p><strong><span class=\"wysiwyg-font-size-large\">When you're ready, email <a href=\"mailto:api@pexels.com\">api@pexels.com</a> with <span class=\"wysiwyg-underline\">ALL</span> of the following:</span></strong></p>\n<ol>\n<li><strong><span class=\"wysiwyg-font-size-large\">A short summary of what your platform is and how our library is being used</span></strong></li>\n<li><strong><span class=\"wysiwyg-font-size-large\">Proof of attribution (either a video demo, screenshots or request a quick call with someone on our team)</span></strong></li>\n<li><strong><span class=\"wysiwyg-font-size-large\">Your API key or the email address you registered with it</span></strong></li>\n</ol>\n<p> </p>\n<p> </p>","user_segment_ids":[]}}